WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.023 --> 00:00:01.520
The most important skill

00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:03.060
of a developer is not

00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:04.323
programming in itself,

00:00:04.323 --> 00:00:05.390
but actually how to use

00:00:05.390 --> 00:00:06.323
Google properly.

00:00:06.323 --> 00:00:07.650
A lot of answers are

00:00:07.650 --> 00:00:09.023
already there on the internet.

00:00:09.023 --> 00:00:10.723
A lot of algorithms are written.

00:00:10.723 --> 00:00:12.123
A lot of libraries are present.

00:00:12.123 --> 00:00:12.923
A lot of things

00:00:12.923 --> 00:00:14.330
Have already been done

00:00:14.330 --> 00:00:16.323
your job as a programmer.

00:00:16.523 --> 00:00:18.630
Mostly is never to come up with

00:00:18.630 --> 00:00:19.810
something innovative or

00:00:19.810 --> 00:00:21.330
something extremely brand-new,

00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:22.630
but your job is to

00:00:22.630 --> 00:00:24.223
glue together, a bunch of

00:00:24.223 --> 00:00:25.950
systems, which are not working

00:00:25.950 --> 00:00:27.190
together initially,

00:00:27.190 --> 00:00:28.223
but your job is to

00:00:28.223 --> 00:00:29.823
just make sure that these

00:00:30.023 --> 00:00:31.223
systems work together.

00:00:31.223 --> 00:00:32.320
You can find these existing

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:33.880
systems, maintained well

00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:34.623
maintained systems

00:00:34.623 --> 00:00:35.800
through Google and you can

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:37.070
find how to link them

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:38.423
together with Google

00:00:38.423 --> 00:00:38.923
as well.

00:00:39.023 --> 00:00:40.680
But most people, I don't know

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:42.323
why shy away from Google.

00:00:42.623 --> 00:00:43.920
I'm the kind of person who will

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:45.690
Google a topic and then

00:00:45.690 --> 00:00:47.023
open 10

00:00:47.023 --> 00:00:49.290
top 10 links in 10, different tabs

00:00:49.290 --> 00:00:51.623
and then take the intersection of

00:00:51.623 --> 00:00:52.323
everyone.

00:00:52.523 --> 00:00:53.023
Why?

00:00:53.023 --> 00:00:54.170
Because this helps me

00:00:54.170 --> 00:00:56.670
to remove the bias from all the

00:00:56.670 --> 00:00:57.323
other people,

00:00:57.523 --> 00:00:58.830
which have written a particular

00:00:58.830 --> 00:00:59.523
piece of content.

